# THE SIFREI ROWS on Numbers 5:1-7:89 (THE NUMBERS WALK sitting 2 — NASO, 2026-09-09): piskaot 1-58 by POSITION, 81 rows at the shelf's
# row grain, each opened and verdicted; the middah named where the row argues by one (logic/MIDDOT.md: I1 a-fortiori, I2 the identity of
# wording, I3 the paradigm, I4 general-particular, I8 the thing that departed to teach on the general, I11 the thing that departed to a
# new matter, I13 two verses reconciled by a third). Two heads mistyped in the export (19 "5:298" = 5:28; 34 "6:150" = 6:15) — found by
# position and asserted in naso_ink.py; filed in RESEARCH_LOG.md.
from naso_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

# ---- piska 1 (5:1-4): the camp purified ----
srow(1, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE WARNING FOR THE PUNISHMENT. Why is the section stated? Num 19:20 gives the PUNISHMENT for defiling the sanctuary (excision, karet — "cut off") but no WARNING; "command the children of Israel that they send out of the camp... and they shall not defile their camps" (5:2-3) IS the warning that the unclean not enter the sanctuary. The operator: 5:3\'s clause is the negative command paired to 19:20\'s penalty — the punishment/warning pairing the courts require (the exam\'s Sanhedrin 54a; Mishnah Makkot 3).')
srow(1, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'FOUR READINGS OF "COMMAND". The imperative is for immediate performance (from the run, 5:4 "and the children of Israel did so") and for the generations (from Lev 24:2-3\'s "eternal statute" on the same verb); R. Yishmael: all the Torah\'s commands take both from the one qualified — a paradigm (I3); R. Yehudah b. Beteira: "command" everywhere means impulsion (Deut 3:28); R. Shimon b. Yochai: "command" everywhere entails expense (Lev 24:2, Num 35:2, 28:2 — one exception, 34:2); Rebbi: "command" everywhere is exhortation (Gen 2:16-17). A DISPUTE on one lemma, four settings RECORDED, none chosen.')
srow(1, 3, 'MATERIAL', 'THE THREE CAMPS AND THE LIMIT OF THE A-FORTIORI. "Out of the camp" — the Levite camp; "outside the camp" adds the Israelite; "their camps in whose midst I dwell" — the Shekhinah\'s (the Presence\'s); the a-fortiori (I1) would have reached the Shekhinah\'s camp from the lighter Israelite camp — so why write it? WE DO NOT PUNISH BY AN A-FORTIORI (the middot\'s own case law — MIDDOT.md). R. Yehudah: the a-fortiori does hold and the clause assigns a SEPARATE CAMP to each kind (the leper alone by Lev 13:46 "solitary shall he sit"); Rebbi: the leper departed from the general to teach on the general (I8) — the graver the uncleanness, the farther the sending. Three teachers, one verse — RECORDED.')
srow(1, 4, 'MATERIAL', 'THE LADDER OF STRINGENCY. The sages\' gradations: wherever the man with a discharge (zav) defiles, the leper defiles, and more (the house-entrant, Lev 14:46) — sent from three camps; wherever the corpse-unclean defiles, the zav defiles, and more (the stone over a cavity, Lev 15:9) — sent from two; wherever one immersed that day (tevul yom) defiles, the corpse-unclean defiles, and more (a man by touch, 19:22) — sent from one; wherever one lacking atonement disqualifies, the tevul yom disqualifies, and more (the heave-offering). A VERDICT TABLE of four ranks from the three camp-words (the exam\'s Mishnah Kelim 1:5-9).')
srow(1, 5, 'MATERIAL', 'WHO IS SENT — THE SCOPE DISPUTED. "From male to female" (5:3): all, not the ark\'s bearers only; R. Yoshiyah: adults and minors (the punishment criterion refused); R. Yochanan: every kind of uncleanness that affects male or female; the one of unknown sex and the hermaphrodite from "outside the camp you shall send them"; the one who cannot walk (carried); UTENSILS from "their camps"; R. Akiva: men and utensils from "send them"; R. Yishmael by induction (a paradigm, I3, from plague-uncleanness — refuted by the couch-and-seat distinction, restored by the leprous house\'s stones); R. Yossi HaGelili: what can become a source of uncleanness (the earthenware vessel excluded). The scope\'s settings RECORDED — the scenes\' who-field.')
srow(1, 6, 'CONTEXT', 'A tangent on Lev 17:15-16 (the carcass-eater who does not bathe): R. Yitzchak — excision for the unbathed body, not the unwashed clothes, by an a-fortiori (I1) from the graver corpse-uncleanness; "if he does not wash his clothes" an exhortation. Not this span\'s verse; the form (the exhortation without a penalty) is row 1\'s.')
srow(1, 7, 'MATERIAL', 'THREE CAMPS FROM THREE CAMP-WORDS; THE SHEKHINAH AMONG THE UNCLEAN. "Outside the camp you shall send them" — not a place inside; from the threefold "camp" (computed on the ink: 5:2 "the camp", 5:3 "outside the camp", "their camps") THEY STATED: three camps — Israel\'s from Jerusalem\'s entrance to the Temple mount, the Levites\' to the courtyard, the Shekhinah\'s inward (the exam\'s Zevachim 116b, routed at Bamidbar); "in whose midst I dwell": beloved are Israel — even unclean, the Shekhinah is among them (Lev 16:16; Num 35:34 — the clause\'s second Torah seat, computed). Onkelos\' "My Shekhinah dwells among them" (5:3) is this row\'s noun.')
srow(1, 8, 'MATERIAL', 'THE RUN\'S DOUBLING READ. 5:4 "and the children of Israel did so... as the LORD spoke to Moses, so did the children of Israel": R. Yossi HaGelili — before the calf there were no zavim or lepers among them; after, there were (the three kinds on the one day); R. Shimon b. Yochai — the fear that came after the calf (Exod 24:17 against 34:30); "did so" — Israel\'s praise; the second clause — THE UNCLEAN THEMSELVES DID NOT PROTEST (the doubled formula computed on the ink: "so" twice, "the children of Israel" twice). The reading of the doubling is the claim; the calf\'s chronology is the tradition\'s, labeled.')

# ---- piska 2 (5:5-7): the confession and the proselyte's theft ----
srow(2, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE RULE OF REPETITION; ME\'ILAH IS LYING; WHO IS GUILTY. Why the section, already at Lev 5:20-26? For THE PROSELYTE\'S STOLEN PROPERTY: sworn against falsely, the proselyte dead without heirs — the principal and the fifth to the priests, the guilt offering to the altar. "THIS IS A RULE IN THE TORAH: any section stated in one place, missing one thing, and repeated elsewhere is repeated only for the thing originated" (the middot\'s case law — MIDDOT.md); R. Akiva: everything in it is expounded; R. Yoshiyah: "a man or a woman" likens a woman to a man for all damages (from the pit, Exod 21:33); R. Yonathan: not needed (Exod 21:34, 22:5 pay regardless) — it teaches its own law for women; "any of the sins of man" — the lie about ANY thing is a lie against the LORD (not Lev 5:21-22\'s list alone); "ME\'ILAH (trespass) IN ALL PLACES IS LYING" — five proof-seats (1 Chr 5:25, Josh 7:1, 1 Chr 10:13, 2 Chr 26:18, Num 5:12) — the lemma Onkelos translates by (5:6, 5:12, 5:27); "that soul shall be guilty": the one of unknown sex, proselytes, servants — minors excluded by an a-fortiori (I1) from idolatry; the heirs exempt from the guilt offering, not from the principal (5:7 "and he shall give it"); THE SABBATH-BURNER PAYS NOTHING — the death penalty absorbs the payment; confession for the guilt offering as for the sin offering; R. Nathan: a paradigm (I3) — all who are executed confess (the exam\'s Mishnah Sanhedrin 6:2).')

# ---- piska 3 (5:7) ----
srow(3, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'HIS OWN SIN; THE THING ITSELF; THE FIFTH\'S BASE DISPUTED; ANY HAND. "Their sin which they did" — not the father\'s (the deposit denied to the depositor\'s son); "restore his guilt at its head": the stolen thing itself may be returned, not money only; "its fifth": R. Yoshiyah — a fifth of the WHOLE (so that it and its fifth make five equal parts — a quarter of the principal); R. Yonathan — a fifth of the principal — A DISPUTE on the fifth\'s base (the exam\'s Bava Metzia 54a; Mishnah Bava Kamma 9:7); "to whom he is liable": the court\'s messenger or the heir too; R. Nathan: the court takes the theft from the robber for the robbed man\'s creditor — "in any manner".')

# ---- piska 4 (5:8) ----
srow(4, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'NO REDEEMER IS THE DEAD PROSELYTE. R. Yishmael: is there a man in Israel without a kinsman? The verse teaches the proselyte who died — the principal and the fifth to the priests, the offering to the altar; R. Nathan: "the man" — a search is made for a man\'s heirs, none for a minor\'s (a minor has no sons); Abba Chanan in R. Eliezer\'s name: the robbed one, not the robber ("to whom to return"); "the guilt restored" = MONEY, the offering being "the ram of atonement"; "the LORD\'s, to the priest": to the OFFICIATING WATCH — not any priest he chooses ("whereby atonement is made for him" — the men who atone).')
srow(4, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'THE PRIEST-THIEF DOES NOT KEEP IT. A priest who robbed the proselyte — does he acquire what is already in his hand? The a-fortiori (I1: if he acquires others\' theft, how much more his own) is REFUTED by the distinction — what he acquires only on coming to hand (tithe) others cannot take; the proselyte\'s theft, in which others have a portion, is taken from him and divided among the watch (R. Nathan\'s phrasing): the middot\'s case law again — an a-fortiori answered by a difference.')
srow(4, 3, 'MATERIAL', 'THE PROSELYTE DIES FIRST. The robber on his way with the money and the offering, the proselyte dies — the heirs exempt from the offering ("whereby atonement shall be made for him" — his death atoned): so R. Akiva taught BEFORE Zifron; AFTER Zifron: money given to the watch, then the proselyte dies — the heirs do not retrieve it ("whatever a man gives to the priest, to him shall it be", 5:10); the priest may not demand the offering from the heir. A teacher\'s two settings, dated by his journey — RECORDED.')
srow(4, 4, 'MATERIAL', 'THE MONEY BEFORE THE RAM; TWO WATCHES. Money to Jehoiarib\'s watch and the offering to Jedaiah\'s — or the reverse: "aside from the ram of atonement whereby atonement shall be made" — no atonement until the money is returned; the living animal is offered by the second watch and another given to the first (the exam\'s Bava Kamma 110a-111a; Mishnah Bava Kamma 9:12).')

# ---- piska 5 (5:9) ----
srow(5, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'EVERY HEAVE-OFFERING; THE FIRST FRUITS\' RECIPIENT. R. Yishmael: a pile dedicated before leveling and redeemed still owes the heave-offering (terumah) — not if redeemed after ("the first of your grain", Deut 18:4); R. Akiva: "all terumah" — a whole granary may be terumah if some is left (Mishnah Terumot 4:5); "of all the holy things": terumah on ALL produce — Issi b. Yehudah\'s a-fortiori (I1) from the tithe, twice; Issi b. Menachem\'s; "which they bring near to the priest, to him shall it be": is terumah BROUGHT? No — Exod 23:19 says the FIRST FRUITS (bikkurim) are brought to the house of the LORD but not to whom: this verse gives them to the priests. The row assigns Exodus\' unassigned bringing its recipient.')

# ---- piska 6 (5:10) ----
srow(6, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'A MAN\'S HOLY THINGS ARE HIS — WHAT STAYS WITH THE OWNER; THE FOURTH-YEAR FRUIT. All holy things were pulled out to the priests, leaving the owners portions of the thank and peace offerings, the paschal lamb, the animal tithe, the second tithe, and the fourth-year planting (neta revai); the officiating priest\'s skin; NETA REVAI to the owners — R. Meir from this verse; R. Shimon by the three-facet analogy with the second tithe (called holy, brought to the place, redeemed) — refuted by terumah (holy, not brought), refuted by first fruits (brought, not redeemed), and restored: "I learn a thing of three facets from a thing similar in three, not from one similar in one or two" (the middot\'s case law on the paradigm\'s strength); R. Yossi from Lev 19:25 "to increase for YOU". Onkelos\' inserted "THE TITHE of his holy things" (5:10) names one item of this row\'s list. The exam: Mishnah Maaser Sheni 5:1-5.')
srow(6, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'NO SEIZING; THE OWNER\'S CHOICE; THE FIRSTBORN\'S THIRTY DAYS. From 18:19 a priest might seize the gifts — "a man\'s holy things are his": he gives to whom he wishes; measured out on the ground for some priests and others joined — the later ones share ("his holy things are his"); in a basket — the first keep it ("whatever a man gives to the priest"); R. Yossi: A SON REDEEMED WITHIN THIRTY DAYS WHO DIES — the money returns ("his holy things are his"); AFTER thirty days — it stays with the priest ("whatever a man gives to the priest, to him shall it be") — the firstborn engine\'s thirty-day row at a Naso seat (Bekhorot 49a, routed at Bamidbar; the compiled cold_run_bamidbar levites(age)).')

# ---- piska 7 (5:12-14): the suspected wife ----
srow(7, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE SECTION\'S PURPOSE: ONE WITNESS OR DOUBT; WHO DRINKS; ME\'ILAH IS LYING. Deut 24:1 covers two witnesses without warning (divorce); one witness, or doubt after warning and secreting — THIS section: she drinks. "A man, a man": the wife of a deaf-mute, an imbecile, one abroad or imprisoned, a dullard — the COURT warns her, to void her marriage contract (ketubah), not to make her drink ("the man shall bring his wife", 5:15); R. Yossi b. Yehudah: to drink too, when the husband returns; the widow awaiting the levir (shomeret yavam) included; "his wife" — fit wives only: excluded the widow to the high priest, the divorcee to a priest, the bastard (mamzeret) or Gibeonite to an Israelite, an Israelite\'s daughter to them; AKAVYA B. MEHALALEL excludes the proselyte and the freed slave — the sages: Shemaya and Avtalyon gave Karkemit the freed slave to drink — he: "they dissimulated" — excommunicated, and the court stoned his coffin (Mishnah Eduyot 5:6 — the exam); "faithless to him": in illicit relations, not money (from 5:13); "me\'ilah in all places is lying" with the five seats again.')
srow(7, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'A MAN, NOT A MINOR; WITH HER, NOT HER SISTER. "And a man lie with her": not a minor; "with her" — not with her sister (the a-fortiori (I1) from the husband\'s lighter bar to the sister\'s lifelong bar REFUTED by the word); Abba Chanan in R. Eliezer\'s name: not the mother-in-law, not any forbidden relation (the same a-fortiori refused). The cohabitor\'s identity limits the ordeal to the WIFE\'S OWN act — a scene field.')
srow(7, 3, 'MATERIAL', 'THE CONDITIONS READ ONE BY ONE; THE MINIMUM TIME\'S SIX SETTINGS; DOUBT AS THE CASE. "Hidden from her husband\'s eyes" — not if he sees and feigns blindness; witnesses to the SECRETING, none to the defiling; THE MINIMUM TIME OF SECRETING — R. Yishmael: the time of intercourse / the first stage (circling a palm); R. Eliezer: pouring a cup; R. Yehoshua: drinking it; Ben Azzai: frying an egg; R. Akiva: swallowing it; R. Yehudah b. Beteira: three eggs in a row — SIX SETTINGS OF ONE PARAMETER (Mishnah Sotah 1:2\'s list; Sotah 4a-b); "witness" = TWO unless "one" is written — a paradigm (I3) from Deut 19:15; "not seized": the forced excluded (the a-fortiori from the lighter widow-to-the-high-priest refused) — but a PRIEST\'S WIFE forbidden even forced; "he warn his wife": R. Yishmael optional / R. Akiva mandatory — DISPUTE; R. Akiva: "and she is defiled" THRICE (5:14, 27, 29) — to her husband, to the cohabitor, to the heave-offering (the ink\'s eight tokens of the root computed); R. Yishmael: the priesthood by an a-fortiori from the divorcee; "defiled... not defiled" in one verse — SHE DRINKS ONLY IN DOUBT, and from the sotah THE DOUBT-RULE OF PURITY: doubt equated with certainty in a PRIVATE DOMAIN for a subject with the intelligence to be questioned; public domain clean; without the intelligence, clean in both (Mishnah Taharot 4:7-11, 6:2 — the exam\'s Sotah 28a-29a).')

# ---- piska 8 (5:15) ----
srow(8, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE HUSBAND BRINGS HER; HER OFFERING; BARLEY MEAL; NO OIL, NO FRANKINCENSE; THE MEMORIAL; MERIT SUSPENDS — FOUR SETTINGS. "The man shall bring his wife": two scholars go with them (Mishnah Sotah 1:3); R. Yossi\'s trust-a-fortiori from the menstruant refuted (the menstruant is permitted afterward, the sotah may not be); "her offering for her": every offering she owes (R. Yehudah) / the sages: what permits her to him he pays (the woman after birth or discharge), what does not (the nazirite\'s, the Sabbath\'s) from her contract; "MEAL" not fine flour, "BARLEY" not wheat — R. Gamliel: as her deeds were a beast\'s, her food a beast\'s (Mishnah Sotah 2:1); oil and frankincense two separate negatives; "jealousies" plural — hers and her husband\'s, below and Above; "A MEMORIAL" — R. Tarfon: the one memorial for punishment; R. Akiva: for merit too (5:28\'s seed); R. Yishmael: GENERAL-PARTICULAR (I4) — "a reminder of sin" specifies the general "memorial" — AND THE MIDDOT\'S CASE LAW: when a general-particular defeats an a-fortiori, if both can be satisfied the a-fortiori is not defeated — so MERIT SUSPENDS the waters: three months (Abba Yossi b. Chanan — the fetus recognizable), nine (R. Eliezer b. Yitzchak of Kfar Darom — "seed"), twelve (R. Yishmael — Daniel 4), NOT AT ALL (R. Shimon b. Yochai — the deterrent diluted, the clean slandered); Rebbi: it suspends and she dies that death in the end; R. Shimon: her face turns green at once and she is rushed out. A PARAMETER, merit_suspends: {0, 3, 9, 12} months — the exam\'s Mishnah Sotah 3:4-5.')

# ---- piskaot 9-14 (5:16-21) ----
srow(9, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'ONE AT A TIME; NOT WITH HER SERVANTS; AT THE NICANOR GATE. "The priest shall bring her near": not two suspected wives together; "stand her": not with her servants — she is brazen before them; "before the LORD": at the Nicanor gate, where the head of the watch stood the unclean (Mishnah Sotah 1:5).')
srow(10, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE LAVER\'S WATER; A NEW EARTHEN VESSEL; THE FLOOR\'S DUST; THREE VISIBLE THINGS. "Holy water" = water consecrated in a vessel, the LAVER\'S (Onkelos\' word); "an earthen vessel" — other vessels not equated (the red-heifer analogy refused by the specification); A NEW ONE by the identity of wording (I2) with Lev 14:5\'s bird-vessel — R. Yishmael; the dust: if none, bring it and lay it — THE PLACE CONSECRATES; Issi b. Yehudah: the Temple\'s floor too ("that shall be"); Issi b. Menachem\'s a-fortiori from the sanctuary\'s equation — the clause forbids bringing dust in a basket; R. Shimon: the identity (I2) with the heifer\'s "dust" (19:17) — VISIBLE ON THE WATER, and dust before water valid; THREE THINGS IN THE TORAH MUST BE VISIBLE: the heifer\'s ash, the sotah\'s dust, the yevamah\'s spittle (Deut 25:9); R. Yishmael adds the bird\'s blood (Lev 14:6) — a data row of visibility (Mishnah Sotah 2:2; Parah 6:1).')
srow(11, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE HAIR UNCOVERED; SHAMED, WITHIN LIMITS; WEARIED TO CONFESSION; BITTER IN THE PRIEST\'S HAND. Stood where she stood before (walked about to weary her); the priest uncovers her hair from behind; R. Yishmael: FROM HERE the daughters of Israel cover their hair (2 Sam 13:19 an intimation) — the exam\'s Ketubot 72a; R. Yehudah: what is becoming is not exposed; white to black, black to ugly, ornaments removed; R. Yochanan b. Beroka: no more than the Torah prescribes; a linen sheet between him and the people; "as she was not solicitous of Heaven\'s honor, we are not of hers" (Mishnah Sotah 1:5-7); all may look but her servants; "into her hands the memorial offering" — Abba Chanan in R. Eliezer\'s name: to weary her to confession — the a-fortiori (I1) to the doers of His will; "in the priest\'s hand the bitter waters": they turn bitter only in the priest\'s hand / bitter by their effect on the body.')
srow(12, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE PRIEST ADJURES; ANY LANGUAGE; HE OPENS FOR MERIT. "The priest shall adjure her" — she does not swear of herself (the identity with Lev 5:4 refused by the verse); "say to the woman": in ANY LANGUAGE she understands — R. Yoshiyah (the a-fortiori from the levirate\'s Hebrew refuted by the verse; Mishnah Sotah 7:1); R. Yonathan: from the two amens (she must understand) — "say to the woman" then teaches that the priest instructs her in the oath\'s order; "if no man has lain with you": HE OPENS FOR MERIT — much wine, much levity, much youth; many were swept away; do not let the Name written in holiness be erased by the waters; he recounts the early writings (Job 15:18) and what is unfit to hear; R. Yishmael: first the waters\' strength — a dry powder on raw flesh, harmless until it finds a wound (Mishnah Sotah 1:4).')
srow(13, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE IRREGULAR MODE; THE IMPOTENT. "If you have gone astray" — the regular mode; "if you are defiled" — the irregular; "a man has put his lying in you" — the impotent (lying without seed) included; "besides your husband" — the impotent husband\'s wife included; he stipulates every contingency.')
srow(14, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'OATH IS CURSE; UNDER THE NAME; KNOWN AMONG HER PEOPLE. "The oath of the curse": Lev 5:1\'s "curse" — by the identity of wording (I2) "curse"/"curse", an oath is equated with a curse there as here, and EVERY OATH IN THE TORAH IS UNDER THE NAME (5:21 "the LORD make you") — the exam\'s Shevuot 35b-36a; "in the midst of your people": your people at peace; not in a foreign land — degraded where one is known.')

# ---- piska 15 (5:22) ----
srow(15, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE ADULTERER\'S BELLY AND THIGH; THE TWO AMENS. R. Yossi HaGelili: 5:22\'s "to swell the belly and make fall the thigh" (belly FIRST — computed) is the ADULTERER\'S, 5:21\'s thigh-then-belly already the adulteress\'s — the punishment overtakes him too; the a-fortiori (I1) from the weaker attribute (punishment) to the stronger (benefaction); "amen, amen": R. Meir — amen that I have not been defiled, amen that I WILL not (the waters retroactive); the sages disagree: amen on the oath, amen on the curse; amen for this man, for another; betrothed, married; awaiting the levir, after him — THE RULE: the conditions must be of the time she is his wife (Mishnah Sotah 2:5).')
srow(15, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'FROM THE SOTAH\'S OATH TO ALL OATHS; THE ROLLED OATH. Since oaths are stated generically and the sotah\'s specifies a curse, the Name, and "amen" — all the Torah\'s oaths take a curse, the Name, and an answered amen; Abba Chanan in R. Eliezer\'s name: the judges\' oath answered by amen, else a vain oath; THE ROLLING OF OATHS (an earlier matter rolled onto the present oath) derived from the sotah for all oaths — and by an a-fortiori (I1) to thefts, where a prior claim exists (the exam\'s Kiddushin 27b-28a; Shevuot 48b).')

# ---- piskaot 16-18 (5:23-27) ----
srow(16, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THESE CURSES; THE PRIEST WRITES; ERASABLE — A SCROLL AND INK; THE HERETICS\' SCROLLS. "These" — not all the covenant\'s curses; "the priest" — not any man (the identity with Deut 24:1\'s divorce-writ refused); "erase" — on the erasable; THE A-FORTIORI (I1): if for peace between a man and his wife the Name written in holiness is erased, how much more the heretics\' scrolls — R. Yishmael cuts out the Names and burns the rest, R. Akiva burns them whole (the exam\'s Shabbat 116a); "into a scroll" — not a tablet, paper or hide but finished parchment; ink, not gum or vitriol — WRITING THAT CAN BE ERASED (Mishnah Sotah 2:4); the writing makes the waters bitter.')
srow(17, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'FROM HER OWN HAND; THE DRINKING TWICE; THREE CATEGORICAL REQUIREMENTS; WAVED AND PRESENTED. "From the woman\'s hand" — not her agent; a menstruant does not drink (barred from the court); the drinking written at 5:24 and again at 5:26-27 — R. Akiva: after the erasure, if she refuses, she is forced; R. Shimon: THREE THINGS ARE CATEGORICAL — the scroll\'s erasure, the fistful\'s offering, her acceptance of the oath; erased, then "I am unclean": the waters spilled, the offering scattered on the ash-heap, the scroll invalid for another (R. Achi b. R. Yoshiyah: valid) — Mishnah Sotah 3:3; "wave": back and forth, up and down (lifting likened to waving by Exod 29:27); "before the LORD": the east; waving AND presentation at the altar\'s corner; the fistful\'s "memorial" is Lev 2:2\'s (the exam\'s Sotah 19a-20b).')
srow(18, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'FROM THE LIMB WHERE THE SIN BEGAN. The other limbs from "the waters enter her"; belly and thigh NAMED because FROM THE LIMB WHENCE THE SIN BEGAN THE PUNISHMENT BEGINS — the flood (Gen 7:23 "from man"), Sodom (19:11 "from small to great"), Pharaoh (Exod 14:4), the condemned city (Deut 13:16) — five seats of one pattern; the a-fortiori (I1) to reward; "a curse in the midst of her people": they curse by her, swear by her (Isa 65:15 — the wicked an oath for the righteous); the righteous a blessing for the nations (Jer 4:2, Gen 12:3, 48:20). The limb rule is a narrative pattern on the punishment\'s FORM — labeled E-series (the 32) rather than a law.')

# ---- piskaot 19-21 (5:28-31) ----
srow(19, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'FOUND BY POSITION (the export heads this row "5:298"; between 18 on 5:27 and 20 on 5:29, quoting "and if the woman had not been defiled" — the row on 5:28; RESEARCH_LOG.md). WHO DEFILED HER THAT SCRIPTURE MUST CLEANSE HER? Lev 20:10: witnesses and warning → death; witnesses without warning → forbidden to her husband (Deut 24:1); DOUBT → this verse: since an evil name went out against her, she is forbidden until she drinks; "she is clean": to her husband, to the cohabitor, to the heave-offering; "absolved": of the curses and the oath; "SHE SHALL BE SOWN WITH SEED": R. Yishmael — the barren conceives (Onkelos\' "she shall conceive a conception" is this arm); R. AKIVA: then every barren woman will secrete herself to conceive and the modest lose — rather, females become males, one becomes two, dark fair, short tall; R. Shimon: reward for transgression? — she was forbidden for seed and is now permitted; variantly: excludes the wombless (ailonit) and the unfit to bear from drinking (Mishnah Sotah 4:3).')
srow(20, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THIS IS THE LAW — THE FIRST OF THREE; THE MAN LIKENED TO THE WOMAN; BETROTHED AND AWAITING THE LEVIR. "This is the law of jealousies": R. Yoshiyah — for the generations (the construct); R. Yonathan — a summation (the same pair on 6:13, 6:21 — three formulas, computed); "a wife under her husband": the woman likened to the man — a blind husband or wife, she does not drink (Mishnah Sotah 4:4?—the exam); the widow awaiting the levir INCLUDED by "a man, a man" and the BETROTHED EXCLUDED by "under her husband" (R. Yoshiyah) — R. Yonathan reverses the two verses (5:19 "under your husband" excludes the awaiting widow; "a wife who goes astray" the betrothed) — DISPUTE on which words exclude whom, the verdict shared (Mishnah Sotah 4:1); "a man, a man" the court\'s warning for the ketubah (row 7:1 again).')
srow(21, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'OBLIGATORY; THE MAN CLEAN OF SIN — THE WATERS TEST ONLY A CLEAN HUSBAND. "Or a man" — 5:30 repeats 5:14 to make the drinking OBLIGATORY, not optional; "the priest shall do to her all this law, and the man shall be clean of sin": if he did so; he should not say "I have killed a daughter of Israel"; Shimon b. Azzai: even a clean woman who secreted herself does not escape punishment ("that woman shall bear her sin"); Rebbi: the defiled one dies that death in the end; variantly — HOSEA 4:14 "I shall not punish your daughters when they commit harlotry, for they themselves...": WHEN THE MAN IS CLEAN OF SIN, the woman bears hers — if the husbands pursue harlotry, the waters do not test their wives (Mishnah Sotah 9:9 — R. Yochanan b. Zakkai abolished the waters when adulterers multiplied; the exam\'s Sotah 47b). A gate on the ordeal: the husband\'s own cleanness.')

# ---- piska 22 (6:1-2): the Nazirite ----
srow(22, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE SECTION\'S PURPOSE: THIRTY DAYS; WOMEN, NOT MINORS; THE AGES OF VOWS; WILLINGLY; HANDLES AND EPITHETS; ANNULLED BY FATHER AND HUSBAND; SHIMON THE RIGHTEOUS\'S NAZIRITE. Against Num 30:3 (a vow binds by its own term): a nazirite vow of one day or one moment binds THIRTY DAYS — the default — and three prohibitions (wine, the dead, the hair); "a man or a woman": women equated (the a-fortiori (I1) from the priests\' minors refuted); "a man": not a minor (the reverse a-fortiori refuted); "if he declares": one who knows to declare — A GIRL OF ELEVEN AND A DAY IS EXAMINED, OF TWELVE AND A DAY HER VOWS STAND; A BOY OF TWELVE AND A DAY EXAMINED, THIRTEEN AND A DAY STAND (Mishnah Niddah 5:6 — the majority engine\'s data row); "declares": willingly, by the identity of wording (I2) with Lev 22:21\'s vows and gifts; "to vow a vow": not an offering-vow; "nazir" — himself, not others; EPITHETS AND HANDLES OF NAZIRSHIP ARE NAZIRSHIP, and vows likened to nazirship both ways (Mishnah Nazir 1:1; Nedarim 1:1); "he shall not profane his word" and "you shall not delay" apply; a father annuls his daughter\'s, a husband his wife\'s (Num 30); R. Yehoshua: even others; "to the LORD" — a mitzvah; SHIMON THE RIGHTEOUS ate one defiled nazirite\'s guilt offering only — the shepherd from the south who saw his reflection and vowed to shear his hair for Heaven (the exam\'s Nedarim 9b, Nazir 4b) — the tail CONTEXT, the rules MATERIAL.')

# ---- piska 23 (6:3) ----
srow(23, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'MITZVAH WINE EQUATED; YAYIN AND SHEKHAR — TWO TONGUES OR DILUTED AND UNDILUTED; SEPARATION; SELLING PERMITTED; VINEGAR; THE TASTE AS THE SUBSTANCE; WET AND DRY. "From wine and strong drink he shall separate": to equate mitzvah wine (the second tithe\'s) with optional wine as forbidden — the mourner analogy refuted, the officiating priest\'s a-fortiori (I1) refuted by the death-penalty distinction, so the verse is needed; R. Yossi HaGelili: against Deut 14:23\'s tithe-wine; Abba Chanan in R. Eliezer\'s name: the corpse-with-no-burier analogy; "yayin and shekhar" — yayin IS shekhar: THE TORAH SPEAKS IN TWO TONGUES (slaughter/sacrifice, fistful/lifting, lowland/plain, sign/wonder) — R. Elazar Hakappar: yayin diluted, shekhar undiluted (Num 28:7\'s "a pouring of shekhar" on the altar) — Onkelos\' "new and old" the third reading, RECORDED beside; "separation" (nezirah) at Lev 22:2, 25:5, Hos 9:10, Zech 7:3; "he shall not DRINK" — selling and healing permitted; VINEGAR equated with wine (the priest\'s a-fortiori refuted); "any steeping of grapes": the TASTE regarded as the substance — A PARADIGM (I3) FOR EVERY TORAH PROHIBITION by an a-fortiori from the nazirite\'s lighter bar (not for all time, not for benefit, releasable) — the exam\'s Pesachim 44b, Nazir 37a; "grapes moist": half-ripe included (the finished-product analogy refuted); "dry": dried; Issi b. Yehudah: each a liability in itself (Mishnah Nazir 6:1-2).')

# ---- piska 24 (6:4) ----
srow(24, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'AN OLIVE\'S BULK COMBINED — FORTY LASHES; LEAVES EXCLUDED; TWO KERNELS, ONE HUSK; WHICH IS WHICH; PAINED EATING; GENERAL-PARTICULAR AND ITS LIMIT. An olive\'s bulk of all combined: forty lashes — COMBINATION a paradigm (I3) for all prohibitions by the same a-fortiori; "of all that is made from the vine" — leaves and sprouts excluded by "from kernels to husk" (fruit and residue of fruit); R. Eliezer includes them; the minimum: two kernels and one husk (R. Elazar b. Azariah — Mishnah Nazir 6:2); WHICH IS WHICH — R. Yehudah: the kernels outer, the husks inner; R. Yossi: as the bell (zog) and its clapper — the husk outer (the exam\'s Nazir 34b); "pained eating" does not exempt (the Yom Kippur a-fortiori refuted); GENERAL-PARTICULAR (I4): "all that is made of the vine" (general), "wine and vinegar" (particular) — fruit and residue of fruit — and THE MIDDOT\'S CASE LAW: a general that ADDS to the particular need not match the particular\'s nature unless Scripture specifies, as it does here.')

# ---- piska 25 (6:5) ----
srow(25, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE VOW CONTINGENT; THE SHAVER AS THE SHAVED; TEARING AND PLUCKING DISPUTED; THIRTY DAYS; THE ETERNAL NAZIRITE; HOLY = THE HAIR; VANDALS; THE HAIRLESS; THIRTY FROM THE LETTERS; THE LEPER\'S LOCKS; THE DAYS AFTER THE TERM — THE A-FORTIORI THAT FAILS. Scripture leaves wine for shaving; the vow contingent on the nazirship, not the reverse; "a blade shall not pass over his head": the one who shaves him liable as he; R. Yoshiyah: forty lashes also for tearing, plucking, trimming ("holy shall he be") — R. Yonathan: the blade alone — DISPUTE (Mishnah Nazir 6:3); an unqualified vow: shaves on the THIRTY-FIRST day, the thirtieth suffices ("until the days are fulfilled"); a hundred days not; the eternal nazirite from "all the days"; "holy shall he be" = the HAIR (6:8 = the body); vandals\' shaving — still holy; R. Yossi: one without hair; R. Yonathan: from "the crown on his head" — with or without hair; UNQUALIFIED NAZIRSHIP IS THIRTY DAYS: the letters of "he shall be" (yihyeh) sum to thirty — a letter-count derivation (the exam\'s Nazir 5a); "let grow the locks": the leper\'s "his head shall be parua" (Lev 13:45) means GROWN LONG by the identity of wording (I2) with the nazirite\'s "pera" (the root\'s six Torah seats computed); THE DAYS AFTER THE TERM BEFORE THE OFFERING equated with the term — for wine (no permitted act in its kind), for shaving (a permitted act — the leper-nazirite\'s — refuted by tumah\'s permitted corpse-with-no-burier, refuted by tumah\'s voiding all) — "I HAVE NOT SUCCEEDED WITH MY A-FORTIORI": the identity (I2) on the EXTRA "nazirite" of 6:20 ("may a nazirite drink wine?") decides — the middot\'s case law: a failed a-fortiori chain, a gezerah shavah on a superfluous word; "let grow" — not less than thirty days; "a month and above" — a month and a day.')

# ---- piska 26 (6:6-7) ----
srow(26, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'A DEAD SOUL IS A MAN; TENT-UNCLEANNESS; NOT FOR KIN, YES FOR THE UNBURIED; THE HIGH PRIEST\'S PARALLEL; IN THEIR DEATH, NOT IN THEIR DISEASE; THE EULOGY; THE CROWN WITH OR WITHOUT HAIR. "Upon a dead soul he shall not come": a human, not a beast (Lev 24:18\'s "soul of a beast" excluded); R. Yishmael: "he shall not COME" — a soul that defiles by entry (Onkelos\' "enter" agrees); "for his father and mother he shall not defile himself" — BUT FOR A CORPSE WITH NO ONE TO BURY IT HE DOES: the a-fortiori (I1) from the high priest refuted by the offering distinction (the nazirite brings one), so the verse is needed; the general rules of the high priest (Lev 21:11) and the common priest compared, the words deciding; R. Akiva on Lev 21:11 ("souls" the distant, "the dead" the kin); "his brother", "his sister": the man going to slaughter his paschal lamb or circumcise his son who hears of a kinsman\'s death — not for kin, yes for the unburied (the exam\'s Berakhot 19b-20a; Nazir 47b-48b); minors cannot vow; "in their death": not in their leprosy or discharge — and the high priest the same by the identity of wording (I2) "his mother"/"his mother"; he may stand at the eulogy and in the mourners\' row; "the crown of his God on his head": with or without hair (R. Yonathan).')

# ---- piskaot 27-30 (6:8-11) ----
srow(27, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'ALL THE DAYS — THE LIFE-LONG NAZIRITE; HOLY IS HE = THE BODY. "All the days of his separation": the interdict on one whose nazirship has no term too; "holy is he to the LORD": holiness of the BODY (the corpse-bar) — 6:5\'s "holy shall he be" is the hair\'s: the two "holy" assigned (computed: the chapter\'s three).')
srow(28, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'CERTAIN DEATH, NOT DOUBT; INADVERTENT AND UNWITTING; WILFUL. "If one die on him" — a certain death, not a doubt (the a-fortiori from the sotah\'s doubt-as-certainty refuted: there inadvertence is not intent, here it is); "of an instant": inadvertence included; "suddenly": unwittingness included — THE TWO LAWS AS A CROSS: the sotah equates doubt with certainty but not inadvertence with intent; the nazirite the reverse — each a-fortiori refuted by the other\'s difference (a paired PARAMETER on two engines); the WILFUL liable — the a-fortiori from the pledge-oath (Lev 5:22) refuted by the lashes distinction, and 6:11 ("he shall atone for him") decides; R. Yonathan swaps: "of an instant" = unwitting, "suddenly" = inadvertent (Mishnah Nazir 3:5?; the exam\'s Nazir 44a).')
srow(28, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'CLEAN THEN UNCLEAN — NOT THE CEMETERY VOW; THE HEAD, NOT THE BODY; THE SEVENTH DAY IS THE SPRINKLING\'S; THE EIGHTH AND AFTER; AT NIGHT; SHAVE, THEN OFFER. "Defile the head of his nazirship": one who was clean and became unclean shaves and offers — not one who vowed in a cemetery (the a-fortiori refuted by the words); "shave his HEAD": not all his hair (the leper analogy refuted by the second shaving; the Levites\' counter-refutation; the word decides); "on the day of his cleansing": the SPRINKLING\'S day, the seventh — not the offering\'s eighth; sprinkled first; the eighth, ninth, tenth valid ("he shall shave it"); the night too; the clean shaving too; and from the juxtaposition with 6:10 THE ORDER: he shaves, then brings the offering — reversed, not fulfilled (Mishnah Nazir 6:9?; Nazir 44b).')
srow(29, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE EIGHTH DAY, NOT THE SEVENTH — NOR THE NINTH EXCLUDED: THE A-FORTIORI REFUTED BY THE PASCHAL WINDOW, THE IDENTITY DECIDES. "On the eighth day he shall bring": excludes the seventh; the ninth? The a-fortiori (if the eighth, near the forbidden seventh, is permitted, how much more the ninth near the permitted) is REFUTED by the paschal lamb\'s time (near the forbidden permitted, after midnight forbidden); from the offered (Lev 22:27\'s eighth day and beyond) — the a-fortiori refuted by the all-offerings distinction; "I HAVE NOT SUCCEEDED WITH REASONING; I DERIVE IT BY THE IDENTITY OF WORDING" (I2): "the eighth day" here and there — the eighth and beyond (the exam\'s Nazir 18a).')
srow(29, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'NO SUBSTITUTION; HIS DUTY TO THE DOOR. "Two turtledoves or two young pigeons": turtledoves not substituted for pigeons nor pigeons for turtledoves (Mishnah Kinnim 2:5); "to the priest, to the door of the tent of meeting": his obligation to bring them to the door.')
srow(30, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'DESIGNATION BY THE PRIEST AND BY THE OWNER; THE SIN AGAINST THE SOUL — DISPUTED; THE DAY THE HEAD IS HALLOWED. "The priest shall make one a sin offering and one a burnt offering": the priest designates; the owner too by an a-fortiori (I1: he who may dedicate may designate) and by Lev 12:8 (the woman after birth designates) — AN UNQUALIFIED PAIR and A QUALIFIED PAIR (Mishnah Kinnim 1:1 — the bird-pair engine\'s two kinds); "he sinned against the soul": HE DEPRIVED HIMSELF OF WINE — and by an a-fortiori the faster who deprives himself of everything (the exam\'s Taanit 11a; Nedarim 10a); R. YISHMAEL: a nazirite who defiled himself — "the soul" a dead one (Onkelos\' "upon the dead" is this arm) — DISPUTE, both RECORDED; "hallow his head on that day": Rebbi — the shaving\'s day; R. Yossi b. Yehudah — the offerings\' day.')

# ---- piska 31 (6:12) ----
srow(31, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE GUILT OFFERING NOT CATEGORICAL — DISPUTED; THE NINETY-NINTH DAY VOIDS ALL, THE HUNDREDTH AND THE FIRST DO NOT; TUMAH VOIDS ALL, SHAVING VOIDS THIRTY; THE LEPER\'S DAYS. "He shall devote... and bring": he may resume before the guilt offering — R. Yishmael son of R. Yochanan b. Beroka: categorical ("when he has brought") — DISPUTE; "the first days shall fall": defiled on the ninety-ninth of a hundred — ALL void; on the hundredth — not ("one who has LATER days voids"); on the first — not ("first DAYS", plural) (Mishnah Nazir 3:3-4); "because his nazirship was defiled": TUMAH VOIDS ALL, SHAVING DOES NOT (the a-fortiori from the shaver\'s equated liability refuted) — shaving voids thirty (Mishnah Nazir 6:5); the leper\'s CONFIRMATION days not counted toward the nazirship — the a-fortiori from the cemetery-vower whose hair is fit for shaving; the counting days likewise.')
srow(31, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'QUARANTINE COUNTED, CONFIRMATION NOT. The leper\'s quarantine days (couch-and-seat uncleanness like confirmation) — refuted: confirmation needs shaving and an offering, quarantine does not — FROM HERE THEY RULED: the leper\'s confirmation and counting days are not counted toward the nazirship; the days of a man\'s or woman\'s discharge and the leper\'s quarantine are counted (Mishnah Nazir 7:3) — a data row of which days count.')
srow(31, 3, 'MATERIAL', 'THE ARGUMENT GOES ROUND AND ROUND — THE IDENTITY DECIDES. "All the days of his separation, upon a dead soul he shall not come" (6:6): the days after the term before the offering equated for TUMAH — from wine (refuted: wine has no permitted act in its kind, tumah has the unburied), from shaving (refuted: the shaver equated, the defiler not), refuted back by wine (the one who gives him to drink not equated, yet equated) — "AND THE ARGUMENT GOES ROUND": the a-fortiori chain (I1) cycles without resolution; "and after, the nazirite may drink wine" (6:20 — "may a nazirite drink wine?" — the extra word) — the identity of wording (I2) "nazirite" (6:12) / "nazirite" (6:20) equates the days for tumah as for wine. The middot\'s case law: a circular a-fortiori fails; the gezerah shavah on an extra word decides (MIDDOT.md).')

# ---- piskaot 32-38 (6:13-21) ----
srow(32, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THIS IS THE LAW — THE SECOND; HE BRINGS HIMSELF (R. YISHMAEL\'S THREE). "This is the law of the nazirite": for the offering of purity, and for the eternal nazirite too; "on the day of the fulfilling" — one with an end; "HE SHALL BRING HIM" (the ink\'s one seat, computed): do others bring him? He brings HIMSELF — one of the three object-markers R. Yishmael reads as reflexive (Lev 22:16 "they shall bear them[selves]", Deut 34:6 "he buried him[self]") — Onkelos\' "he shall bring himself" (6:13) is this reading.')
srow(33, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'WHOLE, THRICE; THREE ANIMALS, EACH A MITZVAH. "Whole" on the lamb, the ewe, the ram — each excludes the blemished; the nazirite requires THREE animals, each a mitzvah in itself (Mishnah Nazir 6:7? — the exam).')
srow(34, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'FOUND BY POSITION (the export heads this row "6:150"; between 33 on 6:14 and 35 on 6:18, quoting "and a basket of unleavened bread" — the row on 6:15; RESEARCH_LOG.md). TWO KINDS, NOT FOUR; LIBATIONS FOR THE VOWED. "A basket of unleavened bread" (general), "fine flour, cakes mixed with oil, wafers" (particular) — GENERAL-PARTICULAR (I4): only what is in the particular — two kinds, not the thank offering\'s four (the analogy refuted by the rule); "their meal offering and their libations": for the burnt and the peace offerings — not the sin and the guilt (the leper\'s a-fortiori refuted by 6:17): THE RAM WAS IN THE GENERAL AND DEPARTED TO TEACH ON THE GENERAL (I8) — offerings brought by vow and gift take libations, the sin and guilt do not; variantly, having departed for the bread, Scripture returned it (the exam\'s Menachot 90b-91a).')
srow(35, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE DOOR IS THE PEACE OFFERING\'S; WHERE HE COOKS, THERE HE SHAVES; THE DOOR OPEN; UNDER ANY OF HIS OFFERINGS; OUTSIDE TOO. "The nazirite shall shave at the door of the tent of meeting": Scripture means AFTER THE PEACE OFFERINGS (whose "at the door" is Lev 3:2\'s) — not literally at the door: an a-fortiori (I1) from Exod 20:23\'s steps (nakedness not revealed on the altar) — how much more no shaving there; R. Yitzchak: from "and take the hair... on the fire under the sacrifice" — IN THE PLACE WHERE HE COOKS IT, THERE HE SHAVES (Onkelos\' inserted "pot", 6:18, sits in that room); Abba Chanan in R. Eliezer\'s name: if the door was not open he would not shave; the hair under the sin and guilt offerings too ("under the sacrifice"); outside the sanctuary too ("on the fire") — Mishnah Nazir 6:8.')
srow(36, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'COOKED WHOLE OR WITH THE RAM; BROKEN INVALID; AFTER THE SHAVING. "The cooked shoulder": cooked WHOLE then separated — R. Shimon b. Yochai: cooked together with the ram (separated before) — DISPUTE; a broken or lacking cake or wafer invalid; "on the nazirite\'s palms after his shaving": the placing after the shaving, the offerings\' bringing not.')
srow(37, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'LIFTING LIKENED TO WAVING; THE EAST; A THING THAT DEPARTED FOR A NEW TEACHING IS NOT RETURNED UNTIL SCRIPTURE RETURNS IT. "The priest shall lift them a lifting": back and forth AND up and down — Exod 29:27\'s "waved... lifted" likens the two (Onkelos\' one verb for both, 5:25, 6:20); "before the LORD": the east unless specified; "holy to the priest beside the breast of waving and the thigh of lifting": the nazirite\'s peace offering was in Lev 7:34\'s general and departed for the SHOULDER — the breast and thigh would follow by an a-fortiori (I1) — so why written? WHATEVER WAS INCLUDED IN A GENERAL AND DEPARTED FROM IT FOR A NEW LEARNING MAY NOT BE RETURNED TO ITS GENERAL UNTIL SCRIPTURE EXPLICITLY RETURNS IT — the eleventh rule of Rabbi Ishmael (I11) stated by the Sifrei on this verse in its own words (MIDDOT.md\'s exemplar).')
srow(38, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THIS IS THE LAW — THE THIRD; THE OFFERING CONTINGENT ON THE NAZIRSHIP; WHAT HIS HAND ATTAINS; FIVE NAZIRSHIPS, FIVE SHAVINGS; THE LEPER-NAZIRITE\'S ONE SHAVING REFUSED. "This is the law": for the generations (R. Yoshiyah) / summation (R. Yonathan); "his offering for his nazirship" — contingent on it, not the reverse; not others\' offering for his nazirship; "aside from what his hand attains": a hundred burnt and peace offerings as vowed — but not sin and guilt offerings ("that he vows" — the vowable kinds); "five nazirships, one shaving" refused ("according to the law of his nazirship" — one shaving each); R. Eliezer b. Shamua and R. Yochanan HaSandlar asked R. Shimon b. Yochai: a clean nazirite who is a leper — one shaving for both? — NO, in every combination: the leper shaves to grow hair, the nazirite to remove it; the leper\'s before the blood, the nazirite\'s after; the unclean nazirite in the counting days shaves after the heifer\'s water, the leper before — a four-way table of refusals (the exam\'s Nazir 60a-61a).')

# ---- piskaot 39-43 (6:22-27): the blessing ----
srow(39, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE SPEECH TO THE PRIESTS; THE HOLY TONGUE; STANDING; RAISED HANDS; THE NAME — IN THE TEMPLE ONLY; ALL ISRAEL; FACE TO FACE; ALOUD; THE PROMPTER. Aaron and his sons are brought into the frame\'s "saying" because the section\'s ACT is theirs — THE RULE: where the speech is to the priests, the act is the priests\'; to Israel, Israel\'s; to all men, the proselytes included; "thus shall you bless": IN THE HOLY TONGUE — by the identity of wording (I2) "bless"/"bless" with Deut 27:12 (R. Yehudah: "answering", "saying", "thus" always mean Hebrew); STANDING — the same identity (R. Nathan: from Deut 10:8 "to stand and minister and bless" — blessing likened to ministering); WITH RAISED HANDS — Lev 9:22 (R. Yonathan\'s objection: there the New Moon, the offering, the high priest — answered by Deut 18:5 "he and his sons": the sons likened to him); WITH THE EXPLICIT NAME — from 6:27 "My name" (the name distinctive to Me), and IN THE TEMPLE ONLY by the identity "place My name"/"place My name there" (1 Kgs 11:36); in the province an epithet — R. Yoshiyah; R. Yonathan: Exod 20:21 inverted, "wherever I am revealed, mention My name" — the Name forbidden in the borders (the exam\'s Sotah 38a; Mishnah Sotah 7:6); women, proselytes, servants from "say to them"; the priests\' own blessing from "I will bless them"; FACE TO FACE; ALOUD; the prayer leader\'s "say" from "say to them" — a verdict table of the blessing\'s form (Sotah 37b-40a).')
srow(40, 1, 'CONTEXT', 'The first verse\'s contents: "bless you" with possessions; "keep you" — ten readings (the body, the evil inclination, all evil, the destroyers, the fathers\' covenant, the end, the soul at death, the feet from Gehinnom, the world to come) with a verse each. Enrichment on the blessing\'s substance; no operator.')
srow(41, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE SHINING FACE = THE SHEKHINAH (R. NATHAN) — ONKELOS\' WORD. "The LORD make His face shine": the light of the eyes; R. NATHAN: the light of the Shekhinah (Isa 60:1-2, Ps 67:2, 118:27); variantly the light of Torah (Prov 6:23); "be gracious to you": in requests (Exod 33:19), in the eyes of men (Joseph, Esther, Daniel), in understanding, in Torah, in gifts of grace — Onkelos renders 6:25\'s "His face" by "His Shekhinah" (computed on the shelf\'s bytes): the translation carries R. Nathan\'s arm; the rest enrichment.')
srow(42, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE LIFTED FACE IS IN PRAYER — LOT\'S. "The LORD lift His face to you": when you stand in prayer, as Gen 19:21 "I have lifted your face" (Lot for Abraham\'s sake) — the a-fortiori (I1): if for Lot for Abraham, how much more for you for your fathers.')
srow(42, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'LIFTS HIS FACE / LIFTS NO FACE — RECONCILED BY A FORK; EIGHT PAIRS ON ONE HINGE; GREAT IS PEACE. 6:26 against Deut 10:17 "who lifts no face": when Israel do His will / when not; variantly BEFORE THE DECREE IS SEALED / AFTER — and the same hinge reconciles seven more pairs (Ps 65:3 / Lam 3:44; Ps 145:18 / 10:1; Lam 3:38 / Dan 9:14; Jer 4:14 / 2:22; Jer 3:22 / 8:4; Isa 55:6 / Ezek 20:3; Ezek 18:32 / 1 Sam 2:25) — A PARAMETER, decree_sealed, with two settings and eight verse-pairs as its answer sheet; variantly this world / the next; "lift" = remove His anger; "peace": in your coming in and going out, with all men — R. Chanina the deputy high priest: in your house; R. Nathan: the peace of David\'s kingdom (Isa 9:6); the peace of Torah (Ps 29:11); GREAT IS PEACE — twenty-odd seats — among them THE NAME WRITTEN IN HOLINESS IS ERASED BY THE BITTER WATERS TO MAKE PEACE BETWEEN A MAN AND HIS WIFE (5:23 — the portion\'s own sotah linked to its own blessing by the shelf); R. Elazar Hakappar: all blessings sealed with peace — the three verses quoted; the celestial peace (Job 25:2) and the a-fortiori to a place of enmity. The fork MATERIAL; the peace-list CONTEXT.')
srow(42, 3, 'CONTEXT', 'MORE CONTRADICTIONS RECONCILED — THE ARITHMETIC ONES. The angels numberless (Job 25:3) / a thousand thousands (Dan 7:10): before and after the exile (Rebbi in Abba b. Yossi\'s name: one host among numberless hosts); the stars counted (Ps 147:4) / called by name at once (Isa 40:26): He calls two names at once, as Exod 20:1 spoke all at once (Ps 62:12; Jer 23:29); the angel\'s name changes with its errand (Judg 13:18); DAVID\'S FIFTY SHEKELS (2 Sam 24:24) / SIX HUNDRED GOLD (1 Chr 21:25): the floor six hundred, the altar\'s place fifty — or fifty from each of TWELVE TRIBES = six hundred (Rebbi in Abba Yossi b. Dostai\'s name) — or the cattle and sledges for fifty (R. Elazar); SOLOMON\'S STABLES 40,000 (1 Kgs 5:6) / 4,000 (2 Chr 9:28): four thousand stables for forty thousand horses; THE SEA\'S 3,000 BATHS (2 Chr 4:5) / 2,000 (1 Kgs 7:26): two thousand wet = three thousand dry — WHENCE THE SAGES: forty se\'ah wet equals two kor dry (a conversion ratio 2:3 — the conversion layer\'s arithmetic on the Prophets\' and Writings\' seats; the exam\'s Eruvin 14b). Not this verse\'s law; the method (two verses reconciled — I13\'s cousin) recorded.')
srow(42, 4, 'CONTEXT', 'A DISPLACED PARAGRAPH (the export\'s own note: to follow 42:2\'s last a-fortiori): the sea\'s shame (Isa 23:4) — the sea, with none of a mother\'s fears, does its Master\'s will (Jer 5:22\'s bound of sand) — how much more you: "be ashamed, O Sidon". Enrichment.')
srow(43, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'PLACE MY NAME = THE EXPLICIT NAME — IN THE TEMPLE; AND I WILL BLESS THEM. "They shall place My name": the Name distinctive to Me, not an epithet; IN THE TEMPLE by the identity of wording (I2) "place My name" / "to place My name there" (Deut 12:5 — the phrase\'s seats computed); in the province with an epithet; "and I will bless them": the PRIESTS blessed too; so that Israel not say their blessing depends on the priests, and the priests not say "we bless Israel" — "I shall bless My people" (Deut 2:7, 15:6, 7:13, 28:12; Ezek 34:14-15) — the blessing\'s agent a data row; Onkelos\' inserted "the BLESSING of My name" (6:27) sits beside this row\'s "the Name itself" — the two members of the spine on the placed thing, RECORDED.')

# ---- piskaot 44-52 (7:1-19): the wagons and the first days ----
srow(44, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE DAY MOSES FINISHED — THE DAY-STACK OF THE FIRST OF NISAN; ANOINTED TOGETHER, INSIDE AND OUT; THE FUTURE VESSELS. All seven days of consecration Moses assembled the tabernacle each morning, anointed it and dismantled it; on the eighth he set it up and did not dismantle (R. Yossi b. R. Yehudah: dismantled the eighth too); Exod 40:17 dates it: from the TWENTY-THIRD OF ADAR the anointing began, on the New Moon of Nisan it was established, on the second the heifer burned, on the third its water sprinkled (8:7); ON THAT DAY the Shekhinah rested (Exod 40:35), the princes offered (7:12 "the first day" — the first of the year\'s days), fire came down (Lev 9:24), NADAB AND ABIHU DIED — their death within, their fall without (R. Yossi: an angel propped them; R. Yishmael: within and dragged out with hooks, Lev 10:4) — THE TAPE\'S CHECK: 7:1 = Exod 40:17 = Lev 9:1 = (2, 1, 1) on the exodus counter, a month BEFORE 1:1\'s (2, 2, 1): the retrograde marker of the compile sitting; the twelve days 1-12 Nisan, the second Passover\'s men on the 14th (Num 9) — one month\'s tape; "anointed and consecrated them": none consecrated until all anointed; inside and outside — R. Yoshiyah: wet-measure vessels both, dry-measure inside only; R. Yonathan: wet inside only, dry neither (Lev 23:17\'s loaves "to the LORD" after baking) — DISPUTE; Rebbi: WITH THESE ALL FUTURE VESSELS WERE CONSECRATED (the sanctuary engine\'s vessels-for-the-generations row, Bamidbar\'s Sanhedrin 16b at its Naso seat).')
srow(45, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'CHIEFS THE SONS OF CHIEFS — THE BEATEN OFFICERS; COVERED WAGONS (REBBI — ONKELOS\' WORD); A WAGON FOR TWO, AN OX FOR ONE; NOT ACCEPTED UNTIL TOLD; WHY FIRST HERE. "The heads of their fathers\' house": not commoners appointed — chiefs the sons of chiefs, the OFFICERS BEATEN IN EGYPT (Exod 5:14 — the beaten foremen become the princes: the corpus\'s Exodus row at its Numbers seat); "six wagons tzav": OPULENT (lacking nothing) — REBBI: COVERED, like covered carts (Isa 66:20\'s litters an intimation) — Onkelos\' "when covered" (7:3, computed) is Rebbi\'s; "a wagon for every two chiefs" — not one each; "an ox for each" — not one for two (the ink\'s 6 and 12, 2 and 1); they stood before the tabernacle and MOSES DID NOT ACCEPT until the Holy Spirit said "take from them — their mind is at one with the Most High\'s"; R. Nathan: why first here and not at the tabernacle\'s work? They had said "let Israel give and we will complete the lack" — the congregation completed everything (Exod 36:7) and the onyx stones were all that remained to them (35:27) — so here they came FIRST (the exam\'s Bamidbar Rabbah 12 — outside scope).')
srow(46, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'MOSES DISTRIBUTED AS HE SAW FIT — TWO AND FOUR, FOUR AND EIGHT; DAVID\'S WATCHES. "Moses took the wagons and the oxen and gave them to the Levites": as he saw fit — two wagons and four oxen to Gershon, four and eight to Merari (7:7-8\'s numbers); and so David distributed the heads of the watches among the priests, sixteen of Eleazar and eight of Ithamar, by lot (1 Chr 24:4-6) — the apportioning act run again in the Writings.')
srow(46, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'ON THE SHOULDER — DAVID\'S ERROR AND RETURN. "To the sons of Kohath he gave none": R. Nathan — this ESCAPED David, who set the ark on a new wagon (1 Sam 6:3 — the Philistines\'; 2 Sam 6: Uzzah smitten, David grieved); Ahitophel: "should you not have learned from Moses your master that the Levites bear the ark only on the shoulder — \'for the service of the holy is upon them, on the shoulder they carry\'?" — so David had it borne on the shoulder (1 Chr 15:11-15 "as Moses had commanded by word of the LORD, on their shoulders with staves") — and "where did he so command? Here"; "they originated nothing, but all from Moses\' mouth, and Moses from the Almighty\'s" (1 Chr 24:19). THE FLOW REVERSED: the Torah\'s rule (7:9) RUN in Samuel and Chronicles, the run\'s failure and repair recorded there — the demonstrate/run law\'s own exhibit (the exam\'s Sotah 35a).')
srow(47, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE ALTAR\'S DEDICATION; MOSES DID NOT KNOW THE ORDER — BY THE JOURNEYING, NOT BY BIRTH; EACH ON HIS DAY. "The chiefs presented the inauguration of the altar on the day it was anointed": donations for the altar as for the tabernacle; presented and NOT ACCEPTED until the Holy One said "let them present"; and MOSES DID NOT KNOW IN WHAT ORDER — by the journeying (Judah first) or by birth (Reuben first) — until told: BY THE JOURNEYING (the ink\'s twelve days = the camp\'s order, computed); nor whether together or each on his day — "each chief on his day", doubled: Nahshon, a king, not to present with each on his day too (7:11\'s doubling computed). The order a decided PARAMETER with its rejected setting recorded.')
srow(48, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE FIRST DAY OF THE YEAR; LINKED TO HIS TRIBE, HIS OWN OFFERING. "The one who presented on the first day": the first of ALL THE DAYS OF THE YEAR — the first of Nisan (the date the tape carries from 7:1); "Nahshon son of Amminadab of the tribe of Judah": to link him with his tribe — not that the tribe gave it — for 7:17 "this is the offering of Nahshon", his own (the day-head\'s form computed: Nahshon alone "of the tribe", untitled).')
srow(49, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'MADE FOR THE OFFERINGS; THE DISH BY THE SANCTUARY SHEKEL; BOTH FULL — EQUAL CAPACITY, UNEQUAL WEIGHT; THE PAN OF GOLD WEIGHED IN SILVER — THE TOTAL DECIDES. "One silver dish": the uniformity of the twelve teaches they were made for the offerings from the start; "seventy shekels by the shekel of the sanctuary" — on the basin; the dish too from "both of them" (R. Chananya son of R. Yehoshua\'s brother: from 7:85\'s "two thousand four hundred by the shekel of the sanctuary" — the total); "both full": equal in CAPACITY though unequal in WEIGHT (the dish\'s plate thick, the basin\'s thin) — a data row on the vessels; the flour donated; "one pan": makes its contents one; "TEN GOLD": of gold with its weight in silver shekels, or of silver weighed in gold? — 7:86\'s "all the gold of the pans, a hundred and twenty" decides: OF GOLD, WEIGHED IN SILVER (the same total the ink\'s arithmetic uses to decide "one, ten" against "eleven" — computed on the accents); "full of incense": donative incense (routed: Menachot 50a).')
srow(50, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'ONE OF EACH — NONE LIKE IT; ITS OWN FIRST YEAR; ALL VALID AS BURNT OFFERINGS. "One young bull... one ram... one lamb": no other like it in its herd; "of its first year": the animal\'s own year, not the world\'s count (the calendar year — Mishnah Parah 1:3; the exam\'s Rosh Hashanah 10a); "for a burnt offering" on the lamb: all three valid — from 7:87 "all the cattle for the burnt offering".')
srow(51, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE SIN OFFERING FOR THE GRAVE OF THE DEPTHS; ALL VALID FOR PEACE; HIS OWN; THE PRINCE\'S FOUR EXCEPTIONS. "One he-goat for a sin offering": to atone for an UNKNOWN uncleanness (a grave in the depths — the exam\'s Horayot 6a? Zevachim 101b); "the sacrifice of the peace offerings": all valid (7:88); "this is the offering of Nahshon": his own, not his tribe\'s; FOUR EXCEPTIONS the prince\'s dedication offering carries against an individual\'s: donative INCENSE (an individual brings none), a SIN OFFERING NOT FOR A SIN, overriding the SABBATH, overriding UNCLEANNESS — a verdict table (Menachot 50a; Moed Katan 9a).')
srow(52, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'HE PRESENTED — REUBEN\'S PROTEST, MOSES\' REBUKE; NETHANEL MERITED IN COUNSEL. "On the second day Nethanel... presented; he presented his offering" (7:18-19\'s doubling, computed — the one block that differs): Reuben came and protested — "enough that Judah preceded me; let me present by birth" — Moses rebuked him: "the Holy One told me — by the order of the journeying" — the word read as an imperative, "PRESENT!"; because Nethanel MERITED IN COUNSEL (he counselled the offerings) Scripture accounts him as if first, and Issachar\'s portion is understanding (1 Chr 12:33; Judg 5:15; the courts in Egypt — Yashuv; Deut 33:18; Gen 25:27\'s tents). The rebuke is the run of row 47\'s decided order; the counsel the tradition\'s, labeled.')

# ---- piskaot 53-58 (7:84-89): the totals and the Voice ----
srow(53, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'ON THE DAY IT WAS ANOINTED = AFTER IT WAS ANOINTED, THE SAME DAY; THE PRIESTS\' GIFTS ON THEIR ANOINTING DAY; UNITED IN MERIT; THE SAME DISHES. 7:84\'s "on the day it was anointed" against 7:88\'s "after": not long after — the same day, after the anointing (the ink\'s two formulas computed); LEV 7:35-36\'s PARALLEL: the priests\' gifts "on the day he anointed them" — commanded at Sinai, ACQUIRED when anointed (the exam\'s Menachot / Zevachim on the gifts\' start); "by the princes of Israel": united in counsel, united in merit; "twelve silver dishes": the very ones donated, none become unfit.')
srow(54, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE DISH BY THE SANCTUARY SHEKEL FROM THE TOTAL; TEMPLE VESSELS WEIGH THE SAME SINGLY AND TOGETHER. "A hundred and thirty each dish" again: the dish by the sanctuary shekel from "all the silver of the vessels, two thousand four hundred by the shekel of the sanctuary" (the ink\'s 12 × 130 + 12 × 70 = 2,400, computed); and TEMPLE VESSELS ARE NOT COMMON VESSELS: common ones weighed singly then together gain or lose; these neither — R. Nathan: melted, recast, no change — a data row on the sanctuary\'s weights (the exam\'s Menachot 89a?).')
srow(55, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'GOLD WEIGHED IN SILVER — THE 120 DECIDES; EACH CREDITED WITH TWELVE. "Twelve golden pans": 7:14\'s "ten gold" — of gold, its weight in silver, decided by "all the gold of the pans, a hundred and twenty" (the ink\'s 12 × 10, computed — the same total that decides the accents\' "one | ten"); the same pans donated, none unfit; and it is accounted to EACH as if he had offered twelve dishes, twelve basins, twelve pans.')
srow(56, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'ALL VALID AS BURNT OFFERINGS; EACH CREDITED WITH TWELVE OF EACH. "All the cattle for the burnt offering: twelve bulls" — all three kinds valid as burnt offerings (against reading "for a burnt offering" on the lamb alone); each credited with twelve bulls, rams, lambs, he-goats; the same animals, none unfit.')
srow(57, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'ALL VALID AS PEACE OFFERINGS; EACH CREDITED WITH TWENTY-FOUR AND SIXTY. "All the cattle of the peace sacrifice": all valid — not oxen alone; each credited with twenty-four oxen, sixty rams, sixty lambs (the export\'s row omits the sixty he-goats the ink counts — 7:88\'s [24, 60, 60, 60] computed; the shelf\'s, not ours); "after it was anointed": as row 53.')
srow(58, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'TWO VERSES CONTRADICT UNTIL A THIRD RECONCILES — MOSES ENTERS, THE VOICE DESCENDS; THIRTEEN UTTERANCES, THIRTEEN EXCLUSIONS OF AARON. Lev 1:1 "from the tent of meeting" against Exod 25:22 "from above the ark-cover": "THIS IS A RULE IN THE TORAH: two verses which contradict each other remain in their place until a third comes and reconciles them" — 7:89 is the third: Moses would enter and stand in the tent, and the Voice would descend from the heaven of heavens to between the two cherubim, and he heard it from within — the thirteenth rule of Rabbi Ishmael (I13) stated on this verse (MIDDOT.md\'s exemplar; the ink\'s three seats computed: Exod 25:22, Num 7:89 share the cherubim clause); R. YEHUDAH B. BETEIRA: THIRTEEN UTTERANCES addressed to Moses AND Aaron, and thirteen EXCLUSIONS — to Moses alone, to tell Aaron: Exod 25:22 (three), 30:6 (two), 31:18, Lev 7:38, Num 7:89 (three — "to speak with Him", "speaking to him", "and He spoke to him"), Lev 1:1, Exod 6:28 (Egypt), Num 3:1 (Sinai) — a COUNT of the exclusion-formulas against the corpus\'s own frame census (the compile\'s check: the thirteen seats enumerable on the ink); Onkelos\' reflexive "speaking itself" (7:89, computed by the points) is this row\'s Voice "speaking to him from within".')
srow(58, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'THE VOICE — GREAT, NOT LOW; THE STILL SMALL VOICE RECONCILED TWO WAYS. "He heard THE Voice": not a low voice — "the voice" explicated elsewhere: Deut 5:19\'s "a great voice", Exod 19:16\'s thunders; against 1 Kgs 19:12\'s "a voice, silent, thin": R. Yoshiyah — when He speaks all are silent (Isa 23:2; Lev 10:3 "and Aaron was silent"); R. Yonathan — He with a great voice, the angels low (Isa 62:6-7) — DISPUTE on the reconciliation, both RECORDED; the Voice\'s volume a parameter of the utterance frames (the exam\'s Yoma 4b: the voice cut off at the door).')
